1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:05,562
A Boeing triple-seven with two hundred and thirty-nine people on board does not just vanish.

2
00:00:05,562 --> 00:00:10,442
And yet, twelve years later, that is exactly what M-H three seven zero did.

3
00:00:11,566 --> 00:00:20,125
So what actually happened to it? Everyone has a theory. A fire. A hijacking. The captain.

4
00:00:20,125 --> 00:00:22,799
A government cover-up. Even aliens.

5
00:00:23,933 --> 00:00:31,412
Tonight, we test every serious theory, and the wildest ones, against the only thing that never lies.

6
00:00:31,412 --> 00:00:32,292
The evidence.

7
00:00:33,433 --> 00:00:38,135
Because the real story of M-H three seven zero is not that we have no answers.

8
00:00:38,135 --> 00:00:42,837
It is that the evidence rules almost all of them out, and quietly points at one.

9
00:00:43,966 --> 00:00:48,250
M-H three seven zero. Every theory, explained.

10
00:00:49,399 --> 00:00:50,966
First, the rules.

11
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:55,155
Any theory has to survive five hard facts.

12
00:00:55,155 --> 00:01:03,176
One: the transponder went dark at one twenty-one in the morning, at the exact blind spot between Malaysian and Vietnamese airspace.

13
00:01:04,299 --> 00:01:12,658
Two: the aircraft then turned around and flew a deliberate, waypoint-by-waypoint path back across the country and up the Strait of Malacca.

14
00:01:13,799 --> 00:01:17,382
Three: at two twenty-five, its satellite unit rebooted.

15
00:01:17,382 --> 00:01:23,203
Powered off, then deliberately back on, for reasons no one has fully explained.

16
00:01:24,333 --> 00:01:32,379
Four: for six more hours it kept answering hourly satellite handshakes, tracing seven arcs deep into the empty southern Indian Ocean.

17
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:37,730
Five: a year later, real wreckage washed up on the shores of Africa.

18
00:01:37,730 --> 00:01:41,311
And a recovered wing flap was not set for a landing.

19
00:01:42,433 --> 00:01:44,437
Hold those five facts in your head.

20
00:01:44,437 --> 00:01:49,590
Every theory you are about to hear lives or dies on how many of them it can explain.

21
00:01:50,733 --> 00:01:54,664
And here is why this case bred so many theories.

22
00:01:54,664 --> 00:01:59,380
When a disaster leaves a clear trail, the wrong explanations die fast.

23
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:02,132
M-H three seven zero left almost none.

24
00:02:02,132 --> 00:02:07,242
Into that vacuum rushed every idea imaginable, from the sober to the insane.

25
00:02:08,366 --> 00:02:11,057
Theory one. The ghost flight.

26
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:15,807
Theory one, and the gentlest. Nobody was in control.

27
00:02:15,807 --> 00:02:26,228
A sudden loss of cabin pressure knocked out everyone on board, and the jet flew on, on autopilot, like a ghost, until the fuel ran dry.

28
00:02:27,366 --> 00:02:31,128
For this to be the answer, the timing has to be brutal.

29
00:02:31,128 --> 00:02:37,397
The crew must lose the ability to act before they can descend to breathable air or turn back to land.

30
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:44,747
One version, raised by pilots and by many of you in the comments, is chillingly specific.

31
00:02:44,747 --> 00:02:46,689
A crew oxygen cylinder ruptures.

32
00:02:46,689 --> 00:02:53,292
The cabin decompresses in seconds, and the crew black out from hypoxia before they can save themselves.

33
00:02:54,433 --> 00:03:02,779
At thirty-five thousand feet, a person has less than a minute of useful consciousness after a sudden decompression.

34
00:03:02,779 --> 00:03:09,271
It is fast, and it is silent. No struggle. No radio call. Just quiet.

35
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:13,163
The case for it is strong.

36
00:03:13,163 --> 00:03:20,070
It explains the silence, the missing mayday, and that long, straight, final flight into nowhere.

37
00:03:20,070 --> 00:03:22,833
It needs no villain at all.

38
00:03:23,966 --> 00:03:26,657
But here is what it cannot explain.

39
00:03:26,657 --> 00:03:33,962
A ghost flight does not carefully turn around, follow navigation waypoints, and thread the blind spot between two countries.

40
00:03:33,962 --> 00:03:38,960
And it does not reboot its own satellite unit. Those look like choices.

41
00:03:40,099 --> 00:03:45,652
And crucially, an unconscious crew cannot reboot a satellite unit at two twenty-five in the morning.

42
00:03:45,652 --> 00:03:49,817
That single event is very hard for any pure-accident theory to swallow.

43
00:03:50,966 --> 00:03:54,872
Verdict: hypoxia may genuinely explain the last six hours.

44
00:03:54,872 --> 00:03:58,777
It struggles badly to explain the first twenty minutes.

45
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:02,173
Theory two. The fire.

46
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:04,505
Theory two. Fire.

47
00:04:04,505 --> 00:04:10,132
A veteran pilot named Chris Goodfellow argued the turn-back was not sinister at all.

48
00:04:10,132 --> 00:04:13,748
It was a crew doing exactly the right thing.

49
00:04:14,866 --> 00:04:20,313
In his theory, a fire breaks out, maybe an overheating tyre or an electrical fault.

50
00:04:20,313 --> 00:04:29,390
The crew turn immediately toward the nearest airport with a long runway, the island of Langkawi, and are overcome by smoke before they can land.

51
00:04:30,533 --> 00:04:32,258
Aviation has seen this before.

52
00:04:32,258 --> 00:04:38,816
Real fires have forced real crews to turn and race for the nearest runway, and sometimes lose that race.

53
00:04:38,816 --> 00:04:41,922
So the idea is not absurd on its face.

54
00:04:43,066 --> 00:04:44,987
It is an elegant idea.

55
00:04:44,987 --> 00:04:49,596
That first turn really does point roughly toward a real emergency airport.

56
00:04:49,596 --> 00:04:53,437
The case for it makes the pilots heroes, not killers.

57
00:04:54,566 --> 00:04:56,587
But the timing betrays it.

58
00:04:56,587 --> 00:05:02,648
The transponder and the reporting system went silent minutes apart, in a clean, ordered sequence.

59
00:05:02,648 --> 00:05:07,497
A fire tearing through an aircraft rarely switches systems off so tidily.

60
00:05:08,633 --> 00:05:10,764
The case against is heavy.

61
00:05:10,764 --> 00:05:19,290
A fire bad enough to kill the crew almost never lets an aircraft fly on, controlled, for six more hours.

62
00:05:19,290 --> 00:05:21,847
The recovered debris showed no fire.

63
00:05:21,847 --> 00:05:27,389
And the systems went dark selectively, not like a spreading blaze. Verdict: unlikely.

64
00:05:28,533 --> 00:05:31,119
Theory three. The cargo.

65
00:05:32,266 --> 00:05:34,230
Theory three. The cargo hold.

66
00:05:34,230 --> 00:05:43,264
M-H three seven zero was carrying around two hundred kilograms of lithium-ion batteries, the same kind that have brought down cargo jets before.

67
00:05:44,399 --> 00:05:46,008
The danger is real.

68
00:05:46,008 --> 00:05:53,646
Lithium fires have destroyed cargo jets, and investigators took this cargo seriously, examining how it was packed and stowed.

69
00:05:54,766 --> 00:06:02,812
The case for: a lithium fire burns intensely, resists extinguishing, and can flood a cabin with toxic smoke in minutes.

70
00:06:03,933 --> 00:06:18,316
The case against: investigators found the batteries were packed to regulation, no fire signature appeared on any recovered debris, and once again, a hold fire does not fly a plane for seven silent hours.

71
00:06:18,316 --> 00:06:19,162
Verdict: unlikely.

72
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:22,886
Theory four. The hijacking.

73
00:06:24,033 --> 00:06:25,160
Theory four. Hijacking.

74
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:31,922
Someone other than the pilots seizes the cockpit and diverts the jet to a destination of their own.

75
00:06:33,066 --> 00:06:40,694
The case for: two passengers had boarded using stolen passports, and for a few days the entire world braced for terrorism.

76
00:06:41,833 --> 00:06:46,480
But after the September eleventh attacks, cockpit doors are reinforced and locked.

77
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:54,999
A hijacking would mean defeating that door, subduing a trained crew, and doing it all without a single alarm reaching the ground.

78
00:06:56,133 --> 00:07:02,799
The case against: those two were quickly identified as Iranian asylum seekers, with no link to the flight.

79
00:07:02,799 --> 00:07:12,799
And a hijacking makes no sense with no claim, no demands, no cause, and an ending in the emptiest ocean on Earth instead of at any destination.

80
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:15,471
Hijackers want something.

81
00:07:15,471 --> 00:07:22,135
This flight asked for nothing, and went nowhere anyone could use. Verdict: unlikely.

82
00:07:23,266 --> 00:07:25,695
Theory five. The captain.

83
00:07:26,833 --> 00:07:32,449
Theory five. The one investigators keep returning to, and the hardest to talk about.

84
00:07:32,449 --> 00:07:38,066
That the diversion was deliberate, carried out by someone who understood this aircraft intimately.

85
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:45,064
Be clear about what this theory actually claims. Not a fault. Not an accident.

86
00:07:45,064 --> 00:07:50,929
A conscious human decision to make an airliner, and every soul on it, disappear.

87
00:07:52,066 --> 00:07:56,537
It fits the evidence uncomfortably well. The turn was flown, not drifted.

88
00:07:56,537 --> 00:08:01,007
Systems went dark in a sequence that looks chosen. The satellite rebooted.

89
00:08:01,007 --> 00:08:07,713
And the jet was steered toward the one place on Earth it would be almost impossible to find.

90
00:08:08,833 --> 00:08:11,777
There is a darker detail investigators examined.

91
00:08:11,777 --> 00:08:21,032
Whoever was flying could have deliberately depressurized the cabin, while breathing from their own oxygen supply, quietly incapacitating everyone else on board.

92
00:08:22,166 --> 00:08:33,477
The radar also showed the aircraft skirting the boundaries between national airspaces, and changing altitude near Penang, almost as if someone were threading the gaps between different countries' radar coverage.

93
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:43,396
Investigators also recovered, from the captain's home flight simulator, fragments of a saved route running deep into the southern Indian Ocean.

94
00:08:43,396 --> 00:08:46,328
Broadly the direction the real aircraft went.

95
00:08:47,466 --> 00:08:54,331
And here is where we choose our words with care, because a real man's name is attached to this.

96
00:08:54,331 --> 00:08:58,305
That simulator held thousands of data points from years of use.

97
00:08:58,305 --> 00:09:03,363
The official investigation stated the route could not be conclusively linked to the flight.

98
00:09:03,363 --> 00:09:06,614
It is a chilling coincidence. It is not proof.

99
00:09:07,733 --> 00:09:13,827
After the simulator data emerged, some reached for details of the captain's personal life as a motive.

100
00:09:13,827 --> 00:09:20,638
But investigators found no clear evidence of intent, and we will not smear a man the evidence never convicted.

101
00:09:20,638 --> 00:09:24,582
The route is a red flag. It is not a confession.

102
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:31,554
No investigation has ever proven that the captain, the first officer, or anyone else deliberately did this.

103
00:09:31,554 --> 00:09:38,787
To declare his guilt would be to claim something the evidence has never established, about a man who cannot answer back.

104
00:09:39,933 --> 00:09:45,262
The official Malaysian report, after everything, reached only one honest conclusion.

105
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:53,087
Verdict: the strongest fit to the evidence we have. And still, officially, unproven.

106
00:09:54,233 --> 00:09:56,741
Theory six. Shot down.

107
00:09:57,866 --> 00:09:59,767
Now the conspiracies. Theory six.

108
00:09:59,767 --> 00:10:08,132
The aircraft was shot down, in a military exercise gone wrong or mistaken for a threat, and the truth was quietly buried.

109
00:10:09,266 --> 00:10:13,359
The case for: militaries across the region were watching that night.

110
00:10:13,359 --> 00:10:21,543
And, as so many of you pointed out, no fighter jets were scrambled to intercept an unidentified aircraft crossing an entire nation.

111
00:10:22,666 --> 00:10:30,641
For a while, investigators could not even rule out that the aircraft had flown NORTH instead, over land, toward central Asia.

112
00:10:30,641 --> 00:10:35,577
But the same Doppler analysis that pointed south ruled the northern path out.

113
00:10:35,577 --> 00:10:38,235
There was no secret landing in Kazakhstan.

114
00:10:39,366 --> 00:10:41,249
The case against is decisive.

115
00:10:41,249 --> 00:10:45,016
A shoot-down over the Strait leaves wreckage there, that night.

116
00:10:45,016 --> 00:10:55,562
But the satellite shows the aircraft flying on for six more hours, and the debris drifted ashore years later from the far southern ocean, thousands of kilometres away.

117
00:10:56,700 --> 00:11:09,567
And for a cover-up to hold, dozens of countries, independent investigators, and Inmarsat's own engineers would all have to lie in perfect concert for over a decade, while planting real wreckage on real beaches.

118
00:11:09,567 --> 00:11:12,974
The simpler answer is almost always the true one.

119
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:19,373
The timeline and the physical evidence both refuse to fit a shoot-down.

120
00:11:19,373 --> 00:11:21,571
Verdict: contradicted by the evidence.

121
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:25,286
Theory seven. Diego Garcia.

122
00:11:26,433 --> 00:11:28,737
Theory seven, a favourite of the internet.

123
00:11:28,737 --> 00:11:36,307
The jet was secretly flown to Diego Garcia, the remote American military base in the middle of the Indian Ocean, and hidden away.

124
00:11:37,433 --> 00:11:43,232
The case for: it is a real, secretive base, sitting in roughly the right ocean.

125
00:11:44,366 --> 00:11:47,349
The theory feeds on a real distrust of secrecy.

126
00:11:47,349 --> 00:11:54,972
If a government wanted to hide something, the logic goes, where better than a base the public is not even allowed to visit.

127
00:11:56,100 --> 00:12:03,089
The case against: the satellite arcs and Doppler analysis put the aircraft thousands of kilometres SOUTH of Diego Garcia.

128
00:12:03,089 --> 00:12:09,344
And a jet that landed intact cannot also shed a barnacle-covered flaperon onto a beach in Réunion.

129
00:12:10,466 --> 00:12:16,997
The wreckage is real. It came from the sea, not from a runway. Verdict: debunked.

130
00:12:18,133 --> 00:12:20,980
Theory eight. The wild file.

131
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:24,636
And then there is the wild file.

132
00:12:24,636 --> 00:12:30,071
That M-H three seven zero was used to stage another disaster. That it was abducted.

133
00:12:30,071 --> 00:12:33,332
That glowing orbs teleported it out of the sky.

134
00:12:34,466 --> 00:12:39,358
Those famous orb videos, showing the jet vanishing in a flash of light?

135
00:12:39,358 --> 00:12:43,874
They were analysed frame by frame and confirmed to be computer-generated hoaxes.

136
00:12:43,874 --> 00:12:46,508
They are not real footage of anything.

137
00:12:47,633 --> 00:12:50,376
And it is worth being kind here.

138
00:12:50,376 --> 00:12:56,253
People reach for orbs and abductions because twelve years of total silence is genuinely unbearable.

139
00:12:56,253 --> 00:13:01,739
The mystery is painfully real. The hoaxes built on top of it are not.

140
00:13:02,866 --> 00:13:07,333
The geopolitical swap theories, the alien abductions, the staged disappearances.

141
00:13:07,333 --> 00:13:11,800
They are seductive precisely because the truth is so incomplete.

142
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:16,267
Where there are no answers, anyone can sell you one.

143
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:21,734
But every one of them crashes into the same rock.

144
00:13:21,734 --> 00:13:30,838
Real, confirmed wreckage from this exact aircraft, washed up by a real ocean, exactly where independent satellite math said to look.

145
00:13:30,838 --> 00:13:33,438
No hoax survives that. Verdict: debunked.

146
00:13:34,566 --> 00:13:35,559
The verdict.

147
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:42,074
So line them all up against our five hard facts. The conspiracies fall immediately.

148
00:13:42,074 --> 00:13:45,528
The debris and the satellite data simply erase them.

149
00:13:46,666 --> 00:13:54,103
The accident theories, fire, batteries, hypoxia, explain the quiet ending, but not the deliberate, precise beginning.

150
00:13:54,103 --> 00:14:00,145
They cover the last six hours, and break on the first twenty minutes.

151
00:14:01,266 --> 00:14:07,927
Only the deliberate-diversion theory explains the turn, the silent sequence, the reboot, and the destination, all together.

152
00:14:07,927 --> 00:14:14,588
That is why investigators keep returning to it, however much they wish they did not have to.

153
00:14:15,733 --> 00:14:18,807
Only one thing fits all five facts at once.

154
00:14:18,807 --> 00:14:29,055
A controlled diversion, by a human hand or a very specific chain of failure, that flew this aircraft into the southern Indian Ocean and ended in a steep, high-speed impact.

155
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:35,009
One honest disagreement survives, even among those who accept the southern ocean.

156
00:14:35,009 --> 00:14:41,421
Did someone glide it down in a controlled ditching, at the controls to the very end?

157
00:14:41,421 --> 00:14:46,631
Or did it dive, steep and unpiloted, the moment the fuel ran out?

158
00:14:47,766 --> 00:14:54,547
The recovered flap, not set for landing, and the steep final satellite signal both point to a fast, uncontrolled impact.

159
00:14:54,547 --> 00:14:59,972
But even this is argued, and it changes where along the arc the wreckage might rest.

160
00:14:59,972 --> 00:15:04,040
It is part of why the search has been so brutally hard.

161
00:15:05,166 --> 00:15:11,105
That is where the evidence points. And it is also, still, where the evidence stops.

162
00:15:11,105 --> 00:15:17,835
Because after twelve years, no one has been able to prove the final step. Who. And why.

163
00:15:18,966 --> 00:15:22,772
So we are left with a strange kind of answer.

164
00:15:22,772 --> 00:15:28,863
We can tell you, with real confidence, what did NOT happen to M-H three seven zero.

165
00:15:28,863 --> 00:15:32,288
We still cannot tell you, with certainty, what did.

166
00:15:33,433 --> 00:15:34,739
The newest lead.

167
00:15:35,866 --> 00:15:38,253
But the case is not closed.

168
00:15:38,253 --> 00:15:44,617
In the deep ocean, sound travels for thousands of kilometres, and underwater microphones are always listening.

169
00:15:45,766 --> 00:15:49,149
For years the search leaned on the satellite arcs alone.

170
00:15:49,149 --> 00:15:52,532
Now, an entirely new kind of evidence is in play.

171
00:15:53,666 --> 00:16:04,163
Scientists went back to the recordings from that night and found a faint, low-frequency signal at a listening station in Australia, arriving from the direction of the seventh arc.

172
00:16:04,163 --> 00:16:06,335
In 2026, they are re-examining it.

173
00:16:07,466 --> 00:16:10,046
It is not the only unofficial lead.

174
00:16:10,046 --> 00:16:17,784
One aerospace engineer claims that faint disturbances in worldwide amateur radio signals can trace the flight path to a specific point.

175
00:16:17,784 --> 00:16:20,732
Official investigators are unconvinced, and it is unproven.

176
00:16:20,732 --> 00:16:24,785
But it shows how many people still refuse to give up.

177
00:16:25,933 --> 00:16:30,169
It is a single, faint signal. A lead, not a location.

178
00:16:30,169 --> 00:16:39,412
But with the search now extended into 2027, it could be the thread that finally pulls M-H three seven zero out of the dark.

179
00:16:40,533 --> 00:16:42,793
Until then, every theory remains just that.

180
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:48,604
And for two hundred and thirty-nine families, the cruelest part is not that there are too few answers.

181
00:16:48,604 --> 00:16:53,124
It is that there are too many, and not one of them is certain.

182
00:16:54,266 --> 00:17:02,077
If you haven't seen it yet, our full breakdown of exactly how M-H three seven zero vanished, minute by minute, is on the channel now.

183
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:04,924
And subscribe to Black Box.

184
00:17:04,924 --> 00:17:14,234
We take the biggest mysteries in history apart, piece by piece, and we tell you the truth, including when the truth is that no one knows yet.

185
00:17:14,234 --> 00:17:16,992
Because the truth is always in the details.

